  "raw_text": "265\n\nUlbi daukan\n \nlilkika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwhiteboard animation video\n \n/ video de\n \nla\n \npizarra\n \nanimada\n\n(Note/Nota: Formerly/\nAnteriormente:\n \nMihta diara paski lilkika\n)\n\nUlbi dingkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nBanhki dingkaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto fill out and put in\n \n/ llenar y poner\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-12/20\n):\n \nPat luki kaikram ki King Lâka Sturka Smalki nani Skulka ra waia dukiara wauhkataya ba banhki\ndingkaia?\n \n–\n \nHave you already considered filling out and submitting the form for School for Kingdom Evangelizers?\n \n/ Ha\nconsiderado ya completar y enviar el formulario de Escuela para Evangelizadores del Reino?)\n\nUlbi sakaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nPrint munaia\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto produce printed material, to publish printed material\n \n/ producir material\nimpreso, publicar material impreso\n\nUlbi sakanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npublication, something produced in writing\n \n/ publicación, algo producido por escrito\n\nBraille ulbi sakanka\n \n–\n \nBraille publication\n \n/ publicación en braille\n\nUls\n \n(v\n-\nimp for both\n \n/ v\n-\nimp para ambos:\n \nUlaia\n \n&\n \nUlbaia\n)\n \n–\n \nwrite, climb, mount, ride, ascend\n \n/ escribe, escriba,\n\nescriban, escala, escale, escalen, monta, monte, monten, asciende, ascienda, asciendan\n\nUlu\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwasp\n \n/ avispa\n\nUmpira\n \n–\n \npoor\n, needy, innocent,\n \nhelpless, lowly\n \n/ pobre, necesitado, inocente, indefenso, humilde\n\nUmpira\n \nlâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npoverty\n \n/ pobreza\n\nUmpirakira\n \n–\n \nvery poor\n \n/ muy pobre\n\nUmpira kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have mercy, to extend mercy\n, to have compassion\n \n/ tener piedad, extender misericordia\n,\n\ntener compasi\nón\n\nUmpira kaikras\n \n–\n \nnot having mercy, not extending mercy\n \n/ no tener piedad, no extender misericordia\n\nUmpira kaikan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmerciful way, mercy\n, compassion\n \n/\n \nde forma\n \nmisericordios\na\n,\n \nmisericordia\n,\n\ncompasión\n\nUmpira kaikan lâka marikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto show mercy, to show compassion\n \n/ mostrar misericordia, mostrar\ncompasión\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-06/19\n):\n \nUmpira kaikan lâka markisa kaka, yawan dîa daukbia apia bara dîa muni?\n \n–\n \nIf we show mercy,\nwhat will we not do and why?\n \n/ Si mostramos misericordia, ¿qué no haremos y por qué?)\n\nUmpira luhpia!\n \n(exp)\n \n–\n \nPoor thing!\n \n/ ¡Pobrecito!, ¡Pobrecita!\n\nUn\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nedge, border, rim, lip\n \n/ borde, labio\n\n(Const:\n \nUni\n \n–\n \nmy lip\n \n/ mi labio;\n \nUnam\n \n–\n \nyour lip\n \n/ tu labio;\n \nAi una\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their lip\n \n/ su labio)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb35\n):\n \nElí prîs tara ba kaikan Ana ini bara ai un nani nikbi turi aisaras kan ba, bara lukan witin ba bla sa\n \n–\n \nHigh Priest Eli\nsaw Hannah crying and her lips shaking but she was not talking, and thought she was drunk\n \n/ El sumo sacerdote Elí vio a Ana\nllorando y sus labios temblando pero no estaba hablando, y pensó que estaba borracha)\n\nKabu un\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nseacoast\n \n/ litoral, costa del mar\n\nUn kahbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto answer, to heed\n \n/ responder, contestar\n\n(Construct:\n \nUni kahbaia\n \n–\n \nto answer me\n \n/ responderme;\n \nUnam kahbaia\n \n–\n \nto answer you\n \n/ responderte;\n \nUna kahbaia\n \n–\n \nto\nanswer him/her/it\n \n/ responderle)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Aiseya 50:2\n):\n \nYang bal winri bara dîa muni upla kum sin uni kahbras kan ba?\n \n–\n \nWhy did no one answer me when\nI called?\n \n/ ¿Por qué nadie me respondió cuando llamé?)\n\nUnmaya\n \n(a/t:\n \nUnamaya\n,\n \nUnmaia\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmoustache, beard\n \n/ barba, bigote\n\nUnhsak\n \n(\nUnsak\n-bh,lv\n; not in / no en:\n \ndict\n,\ndictu\n;\n \nUhnsak\n-dba\n)\n \n–\n \nonly\n \n/ solamente\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n: most usages are with regard to a child\n \n–\n \nLuhpia unsak\n \n–\n \nonly child\n \n/ la mayoría de los usos se refieren a un niño\n \n-\n\nLuhpia unsak\n \n–\n \nhijo\n \nú\nnico\n)\n\nUnmaya\n \n(a/t:\n \nUnamaya\n,\n \nUnmaia\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmoustache, beard\n \n/ barba, bigote\n\nUnsabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto contend, to quarrel, to dispute, to debate, to argue\n \n/ contender, discutir, disputar, debater\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n):\n \nUplika man wal unsabaia want sa\n \n–\n \nThe person wants to argue with you\n \n/ La persona quiere discutir con usted)\n\nUnsaban lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nargument, quarrel, dispute, contention, debate, disagreement, squabble\n \n/ argumento,\ndisputa, contención, debate, desacuerdo\n\nUnta\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbush, wood, woodland, forest, jungle, field, opening, aperture, hole, cavity, rectum, anus\n \n/ arbusto, madera,\nbosque, selva, campo, apertura, agujero, cavidad, recto, ano\n\n(Construct:\n \nUntiki\n;\n \nUntikam\n;\n \nUntika)\n\nBila unta\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nopening, cavity, space\n \n/ abertura, cavidad, espacio\n\nKakma unta\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nnostril\n \n/ fosa nasal\n\nUnta tara\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nforest,\n \n…\n \n/ bosque,\n \n…\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nm\nwb\n-\n05/20\n):\n \nunta tara ami lui ba\n \n–\n \nforest fires\n \n/ incendios forestales\n)",
